Canadian Alcoholometric Tables 1980
Author: Canada Revenue Agency, Government of Canada

  Stillhouse does NOT redistribute these tables. No copy is in this
  repository, in the container image, or in any release artifact.

  Temperature correction — resolving a hydrometer indication to a strength
  at 20 °C — is computed from the "Canadian Alcoholometric Tables 1980",
  published by the Canada Revenue Agency at:

    https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/technical-information/
    excise-duty/tables-alcoholometry/canadian-alcoholometric-tables-1980.html

  Each operator downloads that file themselves and points the server at it
  (STILLHOUSE_ALCOHOLOMETRIC_TABLES; see deploy/README.md). The reader is
  backend/internal/alcoholometry/load.go. Until an operator supplies a
  copy, correction is unavailable and the rest of the application runs
  normally.

  The tables themselves are computed from the OIML general formula
  (International Organization of Legal Metrology, International
  Recommendation No. 22, Fourth International Conference of Legal
  Metrology, October 1972, First Edition 1973).

  Why it works this way: the canada.ca terms at
  https://www.canada.ca/en/transparency/terms.html permit reproduction for
  NON-COMMERCIAL purposes without further permission, but state that
  materials may NOT be reproduced for the purposes of COMMERCIAL
  REDISTRIBUTION without prior written permission from the copyright
  administrator. Shipping the file would therefore put a paid or hosted
  Stillhouse offside. Having the operator supply their own copy keeps
  every distribution of this software unambiguously in the clear, and
  leaves the operator squarely inside the non-commercial permission for
  their own use.

  Fidelity is verified rather than assumed: with ALC_TAB set to a copy of
  the published file, backend/internal/alcoholometry/alcoholometry_test.go
  replays all 117,137 published rows back through the lookup and pins the
  file's SHA-256. That test runs in CI against a freshly downloaded copy.
